# The rungs of the timeline ablations, zipped by their labels: four widths, each trained
# on 20 tokens for every non-embedding parameter of the 2020 baseline at that width
# (gpt3_2020.bux), so every variant at a rung reads the same tokens. The batch follows
# DeepSeek LLM's batch-size law, B = 0.292 C^0.327 tokens, in rows of 2048 rounded to
# 48; the long phase reads an eighth as many rows of 16k, which each mesh splits evenly.
# Use it after the recipe, so that its settings replace the recipe's:
#
#   use gpt3_2020
#   use timeline_code
#   use rungs
d_model = d512: 512  | d768: 768  | d1024: 1024  | d1280: 1280
budget  = d512: 503M | d768: 1.7B | d1024: 4.03B | d1280: 7.86B
batch   = d512: 48   | d768: 96   | d1024: 192   | d1280: 288
mesh    = d512: mesh(data=1) | d768: mesh(data=1) | d1024: mesh(data=2) | d1280: mesh(data=4)
